A||||4||frankshel||automatic door locks||||1||
Z||000000||frankshel||09-03-2001||02:49 PM||||Can I take the auto door lock package, the trunk lock pkg, and power window package out of my 87 and put it in my 85 Fiero?  I think that from time to time I have seen info on this. Before I start removing the items, would someone verify that all of the parts will work?<BR>Also, Thanks for the info on the tachometer filter.<P>Thanks,<BR>Frank Sheldon<BR>Albany (Colonie) NY ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||09-03-2001||04:17 PM||||Yes, you can.  I would recommend swapping doors between the cars.  That way you don't have to drill out rivets that hold the lock actuators and window govenors and then find rivets or bolts to use to remount them.  Of course you must also take the wiring harness for the locks/windows and the one for the power mirrors (if you have that option).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||09-03-2001||06:17 PM||||Once you get new doors and switches, is it possible to just splice into existing wiring to add power accessories instead of changing the entire wiring harness.. I know it is.. I guess the question is, has anyone done it and any hints that would be helpful Should be picking up my doors tomorrow. Already got the trunk actuator and switch...<P>I also have to put my door shells on the new doors. I guess I have to take the entire door apart because of removing the mirror. Hints appreciated for this too.. I know I can search but I was already in this message anyway...<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||mbramble||09-03-2001||08:12 PM||||You need the power window/lock harness.  It is not an integral part of the main cabin wiring, it is a separate harness.  Without it you have no wires to run up to the window switches at the center console, or connectors to connect to them, you don't have the power lock relays, you don't have the connectors to connect the internal wiring to the harnesses in the door.  If you have power mirrors, that is another separate harness.  It also runs up the center console to where the switch mounts.  None of these wires are contained in the main cabin wiring so there is really nothing to "splice in to".<P>With a good schematic, the necessary parts (connectors for the switches, to plug into the power block, lock relay, etc.), and lots of wire and patience, you could do it without having the factory harness(es) but it would not be a lot of fun!!<BR>-------------<BR>I <I>think</I> that I have an extra PM harness if your new doors have power mirrors.  And maybe someone on the Forum has a parts car with the lock/window harness that they don't need.  None of the 5 Fieros in the u-pull-its around here have power options or I would go pull one for you.  You don't rewire the existing wiring, you basically <I>add</I> the necessary wiring harnesses.<BR>-----------<BR>You will probably be transferring your original outer door panels to the new doors anyway???  To do that you have to take out the inner panel anyway.  To remove the mirrors you remove the inner panel and the 'triangular' piece of rubber trim at the top front of the door.  You can then reach down and remove the two nuts that hold on the mirror with an open end wrench.  Most of the ones I have removed have been 10mm nuts but I pulled the mirrors off a car recently and each had one 10mm and one 11mm nut!!  It would also be a good time to replace the dew wipes if they are looking worn.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||09-03-2001||09:09 PM||||Thanks Mike... That will help me tremendously! I'll know more tomorrow when I go check the doors out what I will have or what I will need. Hopefully he will have all of those harnesses... I am imagining a day full of fun changing over the inner and outer panels on the doors!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
